BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 546.42 Tm (deal is is being dishonest and telling people you have other offers when you actually don't." The rule extends) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.20 Tm (to never mentioning real offers either and never asking what competitors charge. Chris Zuiker adds the cost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.97 Tm (of a single careless line: "one sentence may not sell a domain but one sentence can certainly kill a domain") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 500.75 Tm ([3C8uYmkV_aE @ 00:35:23]. The economics check is patience. Alex's outbound Dan deal started March 26) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 485.52 Tm (and closed more than six months later for a small sum, so a quiet thread is not automatically a dead deal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 470.30 Tm (The second trap is inventory nobody will ever outbound successfully. Drew Rosener's tuition bill was "three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.07 Tm (years and and about 300 Grand" for roughly 1,800 domains. Early names like sustainablescallops.com) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.85 Tm (found no buyers because seafood is B2B, low-margin and indifferent to domains [ksUajnoey7I @ 00:21:14].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 424.62 Tm (Brian Harbin puts the carrying cost on the table: about $15 per renewal means "if you got a thousand) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 409.40 Tm (domains your overhead right there is 15 grand," against a passive sell-through of 1-5% [uIsWkqUglS4 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 394.17 Tm (00:12:07]. Jeff Gabriel of Saw.com shows how a broker rejects weak stock in minutes. Robotwrld had no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 378.95 Tm (Ubersuggest volume, only 2018 arXiv results, a "Not exciting" DotDB read, about 10 parked sibling) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 363.72 Tm (extensions and a $200K ask on Atom. Gabriel's verdict: "I don't see many targets, the name isn't great and) Tj ET
