BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 625.87 Tm (Semantic Mastery, sitting on thousands of domains, says flatly they have "never made a penny from a park) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 610.65 Tm (domain," and that panel assumes the parked-page ad money flows to the registrar [eSTvHrvbZ-4 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 595.42 Tm (00:02:35]. Michael Gilmour of ParkLogic runs parking as a scaled business, typically paying 80% to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.20 Tm (owner and keeping 20%, with the fee shown line by line on the dashboard [SE1nkvW6rGw @ 00:21:07].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 564.97 Tm (Back in 2013, Braden Pollock was already telling the DomainFest panel that parking revenue was "going) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 549.75 Tm (into the toilet" and that domainers were "pretty lazy" for sitting on parked names [ZMna4WBn7vc @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 534.52 Tm (00:06:33]. The dividing line is traffic. Gilmour defines a traffic domain as any domain with at least one unique) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 519.30 Tm (visitor per day, and ParkLogic only onboards portfolios already doing $250 a month. David Utke aims) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 504.07 Tm (parking at names with type-in traffic and commercial intent, roughly 50 to 200 visits a month. A portfolio of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 488.85 Tm (untrafficked names lands on Bradley's side of the argument.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 473.62 Tm (Platform selection splits into two playbooks. David Utke tiers providers: GoDaddy CashParking or Sedo for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm (beginners and low-traffic names, Parking Crew or Bodis for proper domainers [ck1VMki_11Q @ 00:01:13].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (The method is manual rotation: test each platform for one to three months, track CPM per domain and ad) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (CTR, move underperformers to another service, and sell the name if every service fails [ck1VMki_11Q @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm (00:01:28]. Domain Notebook runs the same loop in miniature, editing or deleting non-earners, trying another) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm (parking site, then sending the name to auction to recoup cost [ntMgB1hXTa8 @ 00:04:59]. Gilmour calls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm (exactly that A/B-and-lock-in approach "the worst possible solution," because the winning provider changes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (daily. The best provider at the best point in time only wins about 25% of traffic, so any single lock-in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.82 Tm (underperforms roughly 75% of the time [SE1nkvW6rGw @ 00:15:31]. ParkLogic's answer is a meta network.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.60 Tm (It holds each visit for 100 milliseconds and routes it to the highest payer among Sedo, Bodis, ParkingCrew) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.37 Tm (and about 20 global ad networks, with the best Google-backed provider as the floor. The catch is access.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.15 Tm (That auction routing sits behind a $250-per-month revenue threshold and a roughly 98% rejection rate, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 290.92 Tm (small portfolios get pushed back into Utke's manual rotation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.70 Tm (The third fault line is whether a traffic name should be parked at all. At DomainFest, Mike "Zeppy" Zeppelin) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.47 Tm (argued that development converts "domain value to business value." insurancequotes.com earned a few) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.25 Tm (thousand dollars a month parked, then saw 40% of homepage visitors apply once it was built out) Tj ET
